  data:  # 0916
    kind: work_item  # 0916
    title: "What a sketch does with quoted repository prose beyond saying it is data: agent-instruction files, an option that leaves out quoted prose, and a delimiter for inline docstring summaries"  # 0916
    status: todo_hard  # 0916
    priority: 3  # 0916
    parent:  # 0916
    tags:  # 0916
    - sketch  # 0916
    - pre_release_outputs  # 0916
    isbefore: []  # 0916
    duplicate_of: []  # 0916
    not_duplicate_of: []  # 0916
    pr_ref:  # 0916
    description: "Context: option (a) shipped in PR #2203. Every sketch prints QUOTED_TEXT_NOTICE under its title, and SECURITY.md states the position. Three questions were not ruled on.\n\n(b) Files addressed to coding agents (AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md, GEMINI.md, copilot-instructions.md, .cursorrules, .cursor/rules): list them, do not print their content. In the five repositories measured for the PR (httpx, express, ripgrep, mini-redis, knex) none of these files exists, so 0 of 30 sketches print one. The earlier 21-repository study found 2 that print one at 128k (the hypergumbo self-run and mitmproxy), because Additional Files ranks root-level Markdown high (WI-rimip). A name list covers known instances, not the class, so any rule needs a general form with the list added on top.\n\n(c) An option that leaves out all quoted prose: README description, docstring summaries, Additional Files content, and perhaps Source Files Content. Whole quoted files are the bulk of a with-source sketch: on the five repositories the 32k sketch is about 26k to 32k tokens with source against 3.8k to 17k without.\n\nDelimiter for inline docstring summaries. The README description (222 to 297 characters on the five repositories) and the docstring summaries are printed inline with no delimiter. A 32k sketch carries, by a heuristic count of \" — summary\" lines in Entry Points, Source Files and Key Symbols: httpx 50 with source / 56 without; express 46 / 63; ripgrep 131 / 206; mini-redis 81 / 81; knex 52 / 112. A delimiter costs tokens on each of these lines.\n\nAlso open: `explain` prints a symbol's whole docstring as text with no such line, and the JSON outputs carry docstrings as fields. Whether either gets a statement is not ruled."  # 0916
    fields: {}  # 0916
- op: discuss  # f60a
  at: '2026-11-19T04:31:28Z'  # f60a
  by: agent  # f60a
  actor: jgstern_agent  # f60a
  clock: 2  # f60a
  nonce: f60a  # f60a
  message: "OWNER RULING 2026-11-19 (in session): the owner adopted all recommendations of the 11-19 review (three read-only research passes over the ADRs, the spec and the code; record ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/after_fast_smart_test_grouping.md). For this item:\n(b) YES: files a coding-agent tool loads as instructions are listed with the reason their content is held back, never printed; recognised by the tool that reads them (a data catalogue, as main-functions.yaml), following their @path imports (CLAUDE.md -> AGENTS.md). (c) REFUSED, a decision: no option that leaves out all quoted prose; --no-source already removes the whole-file sections, the bulk of it. Re-open trigger: a user or consumer asks for it, or a real repository where injected text reaches a reader through --no-source output. (d) REFUSED: no delimiter on inline docstring summaries without an A/B showing it lowers how often a model obeys an injected docstring (cost: 46-206 lines per 32k sketch). (e) explain prints sketch.QUOTED_TEXT_NOTICE (it prints whole docstrings into a model's context); the JSON gets no inline line, the schema and spec field descriptions call docstring/README fields untrusted repository text."  # f60a
